YY3568 rk chainloader U-Boot source
===================================

This tree is official U-Boot v2026.07 at commit
ece349ade2973e220f524ce59e59711cc919263f with the board files derived from
Armbian commit a710f6715cc06fc90dfdd69fb93d642c52f3a3b8 and this board-scoped
overlay applied.

To reproduce the configuration from an extracted rk release bundle:

  make CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu- youyeetoo-yy3568-rk3568_defconfig
  scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh -m .config configs/yy3568-chainload.config
  make CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu- olddefconfig
  BL31=../../loaders/rk3568_bl31_v1.46.elf \
    ROCKCHIP_TPL=../../loaders/rk3568_ddr_1560MHz_v1.25.bin \
    make CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu- all

The SD payload is the resulting `u-boot-rockchip.bin`. Write that complete
binman image at the Rockchip 32 KiB offset; do not wrap the rk first stage and
U-Boot FIT in another `mkimage -T rksd` container.

To reproduce the NVMe-only SD variant, start from a second clean extraction of
this same source archive and merge both fragments, in this order:

  make CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu- youyeetoo-yy3568-rk3568_defconfig
  scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh -m .config configs/yy3568-chainload.config \
    configs/yy3568-sd-nvme-only.config
  make CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu- olddefconfig
  BL31=../../loaders/rk3568_bl31_v1.46.elf \
    ROCKCHIP_TPL=../../loaders/rk3568_ddr_1560MHz_v1.25.bin \
    make CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu- all

The U-Boot DTS override keeps the RK3568 PCIe 3 PHY in its default aggregated
x2 mode for `pcie3x2`; a `data-lanes` mapping would enable x1+x1 bifurcation.
GPIO3_A7 drives the external PCIe clock-buffer enable active-low, matching the
manufacturer's YY3568 storage documentation; adding `enable-active-high` turns
off the reference clock and makes the RK3568 PCIe PHY time out with status
0x6890000. It preserves the YY3568 storage, PMIC, UART2, and regulator data. It
also enables the board's JEDEC SPI NOR using the reviewed SFC pinmux and forces
inline FIT payload data because rk's first stage rejects external
data-position/data-offset layouts.

YY3568 PCIe power and clock-enable reference:
https://wiki.youyeetoo.cn/zh/YY3568/OUSTORAGE

Before creating this source snapshot, the repository build applies the two
upstream U-Boot PCIe fixes listed by the board manifest. They enable the
Rockchip controller clocks before PHY initialization and remove two unbalanced
`clk_release_bulk()` calls. These are required by the pinned v2026.07 source,
whose original ordering can attempt to lock the RK3568 PHY PLL while its
reference-clock path is still off.

Upstream submissions:
https://lists.u-boot-project.org/pipermail/u-boot/2026-May/619272.html
https://www.mail-archive.com/u-boot@lists.denx.de/msg574897.html

Mainline loads BL33 at 0x00800000 and starts with its stack below 0x03f00000.
The board-local include/configs/evb_rk3568.h selects removable SD, NVMe, eMMC,
SCSI, USB, PXE, then DHCP. The chainload config keeps a three-second UART
interruption window and sets the Linux DTB name to rockchip/rk3568-yy3568.dtb.
SPI commands remain interactive and SPI is not an automatic OS target.
The NVMe-only fragment replaces the default command with
`bootflow scan -lb nvme`; if that scan fails, U-Boot returns to its prompt.
